// ymux's zellij configuration.
//
// Companion to ymux-tmux.conf, which does the same job for the other
// multiplexer. Pointed at by the ZELLIJ_CONFIG_FILE env var that
// spawn_local_pty sets on the pane's shell — and its DIRECTORY by
// ZELLIJ_CONFIG_DIR, which is what makes `default_layout` below resolve. Env
// vars rather than flags so nothing has to be quoted into a command line, and
// the user's own zellij config is left untouched.
//
// SMALL, BUT NO LONGER ONE LINE (2026-08-20). The header here used to say
// "KEEP THIS SMALL — deliberately one option", and that was written when the
// file held only `pane_frames false`. The bar has not been lowered, it has
// been named: every key below buys one piece of a single invariant.
//
//     1 ymux pane == 1 zellij session == 1 tab == exactly 1 zellij pane,
//     with zero zellij chrome.
//
// Zellij is a PERSISTENCE LAYER underneath a ymux pane, not a multiplexer the
// user drives. ymux owns tabs, splits and the window; zellij owns the pane's
// scrollback and — since it holds the alt screen — the wheel that reaches it.
// A key earns its place here only if the invariant breaks without it — and
// note this file REPLACES the user's own config, it does not merge with it.

// A ymux pane already draws its own header, and each zellij session sits
// inside exactly one of them — so the frame duplicates the title, costs two
// columns on every side, and adds a SCROLL counter nobody reads.
//
// It also actively broke RTL. The frame puts a vertical bar at both edges of
// EVERY row, which makes every row look like a table row to the per-row
// direction pass: the whole screen merged into one direction block, and three
// Hebrew letters in Claude Code's cwd flipped 13 of 15 rows to RTL — the
// mirrored-English screenshot from 2026-08-19. `stripPaneFrame` in
// app/src/textDirection.ts defends against that for any framed TUI; this
// removes ymux's own contribution to it at the source.
pane_frames false

// `pane_frames false` above removes the border AROUND a pane. It does NOT
// remove the two PLUGIN ROWS that zellij's default layout puts above and
// below it — captured with `zellij setup --dump-layout default`:
//
//     layout {
//         pane size=1 borderless=true { plugin location="tab-bar" }
//         pane
//         pane size=1 borderless=true { plugin location="status-bar" }
//     }
//
// That is why "the frame is still there" survived the line above for a day.
// layouts/ymux.kdl is a bare `pane`; this key is what selects it.
//
// By NAME, never by path: the layout is looked up in
// <ZELLIJ_CONFIG_DIR>/layouts, and a bundled file cannot know its own install
// path. (Requires restart — i.e. read when the session is CREATED, which is
// the moment ymux creates it.)
default_layout "ymux"

// Zero keybinds. Not fewer — zero.
//
// Every zellij default is a key STOLEN from the program running inside the
// pane: Ctrl-o, Ctrl-p, Ctrl-n, Ctrl-t, Ctrl-h, Ctrl-s, Ctrl-g. In a pane
// that is one shell and nothing else, every one of them is a bug — Ctrl-o
// alone is bash's operate-and-get-next, and Ctrl-s/Ctrl-t matter to readline
// and to Claude Code. It also closes the split: Ctrl-p n used to open a
// second pane with no frame to separate it from the first.
//
// Nothing in ymux needs a zellij key. Detach kills the PTY (the zellij CLIENT
// dies, the session survives); Kill runs a child process; the connect wizard
// uses `action write-chars`, which is IPC to the server and bypasses input
// modes entirely.
//
// This is why `mouse_mode` below is TRUE. With no keybinds there is no scroll
// mode, so the wheel is the only way left to reach zellij's scrollback — and
// zellij holds the alt screen, so xterm.js's own wheel reaches nothing.
//
// The empty body is REQUIRED, not decoration: `keybinds clear-defaults=true`
// with no children fails to parse — "keybindings with no children", caught by
// `zellij setup --check` on 2026-08-20 before this ever reached a pane.
keybinds clear-defaults=true {
}

// Second lock on the same door. With keybinds cleared there is nothing left
// to intercept, but locked mode means a binding a future zellij ships as
// un-clearable still does not fire. It changes nothing on screen: the mode
// indicator is drawn by the status-bar plugin, which this layout never loads.
//
// NOT marked "(Requires restart)" upstream — it applies per client attach.
default_mode "locked"

// zellij owns the wheel, because it owns the only scrollback this pane has.
//
// This key has now been argued both ways in one day, so here is the whole
// reasoning in one place.
//
// It was first set to `false` on the theory that xterm.js owns the wheel and
// the selection. Half right: xterm.js does own selection, but its wheel scrolls
// its NORMAL buffer, and zellij holds the alt screen — so with keybinds cleared
// (no scroll mode) and the mouse withheld, a zellij pane had no way to scroll
// back at all. That is not a trade, it is a missing feature.
//
// The tmux side took the same bet (`set -g mouse on` on attach, decision O-3
// in docs/MOUSE-DEBUG.md) and reversed it on 2026-09-08 (Phase 91.B): tmux's
// left-click capture was landing on Claude Code's redraws, and tmux has a
// keyboard scrollback to fall back on. zellij does not — with keybinds
// cleared there is no scroll mode — so `true` stays here on its own merits.
//
// What it costs, and why each cost is covered:
//   - zellij captures drag-select, so a plain drag copies through
//     `copy_on_select` (default true) and OSC 52. With keybinds cleared that is
//     the ONLY way to copy inside the pane, so leaving copy_on_select alone is
//     load-bearing, not laziness.
//   - a native xterm.js selection still works with SHIFT held.
//   - mouse-tracking escapes can leak into the bare shell when the multiplexer
//     exits uncleanly. Already handled, transport-agnostically: `resetMouseModes()`
//     runs on connect and on pty:exit (docs/MOUSE-DEBUG.md).
//
// The Hebrew that OSC 52 hands back is VISUAL order in a Claude pane; it is
// un-reversed on the way to the clipboard by app/src/copyBidi.ts. Owning the
// mouse was never the blocker for that — ClipboardAddon has always routed
// OSC 52 through our own provider.
// (Requires restart.)
mouse_mode true

// Both of these can put content in a fresh session that ymux never asked for.
// The release-notes pane on the first run after a zellij upgrade breaks
// "exactly one pane" outright.
show_release_notes false
show_startup_tips false
